   "evidence": "Beta.lean:61-63 `mellinDisConvergent_rpow_mul_one_sub_rpow_iff ... \u2194 0 < N.re + a - 1 \u2227 0 < b` with no hypotheses; Beta.lean:118-120 proof is `rw [mellinDisConvergent_congr (eqOn_betaPDFReal a b), mellinDisConvergent_const_mul_iff (one_div_ne_zero hab), mellinDisConvergent_rpow_mul_one_sub_rpow_iff, and_iff_left hb]` \u2014 `hb` is used only in that last step, and `mellinDisConvergent_const_mul_iff` (Mellin.lean:154) needs only `c \u2260 0`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/Convolution/Beta.lean",
   "fix": "State `theorem mellinDisConvergent_betaPDFReal_iff {a b : \u211d} (hab : ProbabilityTheory.beta a b \u2260 0) {N : \u2102} : MellinDisConvergent (ProbabilityTheory.betaPDFReal a b) N \u2194 0 < N.re + a - 1 \u2227 0 < b`, i.e. drop the `hb` binder and the final `and_iff_left hb` from the rewrite chain; the rest of the proof is unchanged. `hab` must stay (at `beta a b = 0` the density is identically zero).",
   "issue": "`mellinDisConvergent_betaPDFReal_iff` assumes `hb : 0 < b` and drops it from the conclusion, giving a weaker statement than the file's own `mellinDisConvergent_rpow_mul_one_sub_rpow_iff` (line 61), which has no hypotheses and concludes `0 < N.re + a - 1 \u2227 0 < b`. With `beta a b \u2260 0` the density is a nonzero constant multiple of the kernel on `Ioo 0 1` for every `b`, so `0 < b` need not be assumed; as stated the lemma cannot be used to conclude divergence when the sign of `b` is unknown, nor to derive `0 < b` from convergence.",
   "line": "115"
  }
 ],
